WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
A stranger asks directions. A door crosses between two people.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Behind it, the person asking is replaced.
In one small experiment, eight of fifteen people did not report noticing the switch.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
That is remarkable. But it does not mean our eyes are useless
or that a twelve-minute audio recording can repair attention.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The experiment tested what pedestrians saw during one brief interruption.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
A meditation product has a different question to answer:
what does the exact recording do, compared with something simpler?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Before buying, try a free twelve-minute routine
and ask for evidence about the product itself.
